%% alt: Four ways to adapt a model. From a base model: supervised fine-tuning on examples of good output, optionally followed by preference tuning on better-versus-worse pairs, or reinforcement fine-tuning where a grader scores attempts. From a large teacher model: distillation, where the teacher's answers train a small student. Each result must beat the eval baseline before it is hosted, versioned and re-validated.
flowchart TB
  B[Base model]:::model --> SFT[Supervised fine-tuning<br/>examples of good output]:::tool
  SFT --> PREF[Preference tuning<br/>better vs worse pairs]:::tool
  B --> RFT[Reinforcement fine-tuning<br/>a grader scores attempts]:::tool
  T[Large teacher model]:::model --> DIST[Distillation<br/>teacher trains a small student]:::tool
  PREF & RFT & DIST --> E{Beats the eval<br/>baseline?}:::control
  SFT --> E
  E --> H[Host, version,<br/>re-validate]:::tool
